diff --git a/FORK.md b/FORK.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..92cb9f937
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FORK.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# Fork notes — type-ahead recursive search
+
+This is a fork of **Thunar 4.18.11** (upstream tag `thunar-4.18.11`, released
+2024-07-30) carrying one feature that upstream does not have:
+
+> Typing a printable character into a focused Thunar window immediately starts a
+> search for that text, the way Nautilus/GNOME Files does it — no `Ctrl+F` first.
+
+Upstream Thunar 4.18 reacts to typing with the GTK views' *interactive search*,
+which only moves the cursor to the next matching name **in the current folder**.
+After this change, the keystroke is instead pushed into the location bar's search
+entry, which drives Thunar's regular search. That search descends into
+subfolders according to the existing **Include subfolders** preference
+(`misc-recursive-search`), so the default behaviour is a recursive search.
+
+## Branch layout
+
+| ref | meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `thunar-4.18.11` | pristine upstream release, the fork point |
+| `fork/4.18.11-typeahead` | this fork |
+| `origin` | `https://gitlab.xfce.org/xfce/thunar.git` |
+
+`git diff thunar-4.18.11..fork/4.18.11-typeahead` is the whole fork.
+
+## What changed
+
+* `thunar/thunar-window.c`
+  * `thunar_window_type_ahead_search()` — a `key-press-event` handler on the
+    window which converts a plain printable keystroke into a search query.
+  * `thunar_window_set_search_button_active()` — small helper to toggle the
+    search toolbar item without re-entering `thunar_window_action_search()`.
+  * the handler is connected in `thunar_window_init()` *after*
+    `thunar_window_location_toolbar_create()`, so the user-defined custom-action
+    (UCA) shortcuts registered there keep priority over plain characters.
+* `thunar/thunar-preferences.c` — new boolean preference
+  `misc-type-ahead-search` (xfconf `/misc-type-ahead-search`), default `TRUE`.
+* `thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c` — a **Search as you type** check box in
+  *Preferences → Advanced → Search*, above *Include subfolders*.
+
+## What is deliberately left alone
+
+The handler bails out — and the key press takes its normal course — when
+
+* the preference is off,
+* any modifier other than `Shift` is held,
+* the key does not produce a printable character (`Escape`, `Delete`, `F2`,
+  arrows, …) or produces whitespace (`Space` still toggles the selection),
+* the keystroke matches an accelerator in the window's accel group, or a Thunar
+  custom action's shortcut,
+* `/`, `~` are typed — these keep opening the location bar,
+* the keyboard focus is in a `GtkEditable`/`GtkTextView`, which covers the
+  location bar, the search entry itself and inline renaming.
+
+## Why 4.18.11 and not 4.20.x
+
+Thunar 4.20 and newer require `exo-2 >= 4.19.0`; Ubuntu 24.04 (this machine)
+ships exo 4.18.0 as part of Xfce 4.18, so 4.20 cannot be built or run here
+without replacing core Xfce libraries system-wide. 4.18.11 is the last release of
+the series that matches this desktop's library stack. See
+`../docs/01-version-selection.md`.
diff --git a/thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c b/thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c
index 6e330b35e..aff1d57b9 100644
--- a/thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c
+++ b/thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c
@@ -1148,6 +1148,23 @@ thunar_preferences_dialog_init (ThunarPreferencesDialog *dialog)
   gtk_grid_set_column_homogeneous (GTK_GRID (grid), TRUE);
   gtk_widget_show (grid);
 
+  button = gtk_check_button_new_with_mnemonic (_("Search as you _type"));
+  g_object_bind_property (G_OBJECT (dialog->preferences),
+                          "misc-type-ahead-search",
+                          G_OBJECT (button),
+                          "active",
+                          G_BINDING_BIDIRECTIONAL | G_BINDING_SYNC_CREATE);
+  gtk_widget_set_tooltip_text (button,
+                               _("Select this option to start searching as soon as you type in a Thunar window, "
+                                 "without pressing Ctrl+F first. Without it, typing jumps to the next matching "
+                                 "name in the current folder instead."));
+  gtk_widget_set_hexpand (button, TRUE);
+  gtk_grid_attach (GTK_GRID (grid), button, 0, row, 2, 1);
+  gtk_widget_show (button);
+
+  /* next row */
+  row++;
+
   label = gtk_label_new_with_mnemonic (_("Include subfolders:"));
   gtk_label_set_xalign (GTK_LABEL (label), 0.0f);
   gtk_grid_attach (GTK_GRID (grid), label, 0, row, 1, 1);
